    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "An inverse-variation table must keep the same product in every column.\n\nIf M=15 and N=−4, then MN=−60.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So if M=−6, N must be 10 because (−6)(10)=−60.\n\nSigns matter as much as the numbers.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
